-- C24 example: injection next to a critically stressed fault - fault mechanics and induced seismicity IN the run.
-- Strike-slip stress state (Sv 0.24 bar/m, Shmin 0.65 Sv, SHmax 1.10 Sv at 60 deg from x): the vertical fault F1
-- (x-faces between columns 15 and 16, all layers) lies at 30 deg to SHmax and starts ~6 bar below Coulomb failure.
-- A water injector 2 cells west of the fault raises the pressure; the run computes per fault face: Coulomb stress,
-- slip tendency, Dieterich seismicity rate and a stochastic event catalogue; reactivated faces become 20x more
-- transmissive (two-way coupling, FAULTMECH item 9) and a quasi-dynamic rate-and-state trace runs on layer 3 after
-- the run (FAULTRSF). Results: 3D view (fault faces + events), Results > Faults & seismicity.
-- OPM Flow / ECLIPSE ignore the '-- RESSIM:' lines (the deck runs there as a plain injection case).
RUNSPEC
TITLE
Injection near a critically stressed fault (C24 fault mechanics + seismicity)
DIMENS
 30 20 5 /
OIL
WATER
METRIC
TABDIMS
 1 1 20 20 /
WELLDIMS
 2 5 1 2 /
FAULTDIM
 1 /
START
 1 JAN 2026 /
GRID
DX
 3000*50 /
DY
 3000*50 /
DZ
 3000*10 /
TOPS
 600*1975 /
PORO
 3000*0.15 /
PERMX
 3000*50 /
PERMY
 3000*50 /
PERMZ
 3000*5 /
FAULTS
 'F1' 15 15 1 20 1 5 'X' /
/
MULTFLT
 'F1' 0.05 /
/
-- RESSIM: STRESSFIELD 0.24 0.65 1.10 60 0.5 0
-- RESSIM: FAULTMECH F1 0.6 0 0 100 5 1.0 -1.0 20
-- RESSIM: FAULTRSF F1 3 0.010 0.015 1.0
PROPS
